### Page 2 of 3

```text
Planning Commission
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
January 11, 2024
applicant revise the overall lot density to comply with the land use regulations in the
final plat submission. A D.E.Q. Chapter 23 non-adverse recommendation has been
received. .
Casey Palma, applicants agent, was introduced and said the development was
reconfigured when an Outside Users Agreement with the City was not approved.
Individual wells and septic systems will serve the subdivision.
Public notification was completed and the only comment received was an inquiry into
how Lot 16 would be accessed. Agency review comments have been addressed and
plat corrections made, including the potential vacation of a portion of Buck Brush
Road.
Chairman Caughey opened the hearing for Public Comments on the Ironhorse, 3rd
Filing Subdivision and Plat. Mike Cahoon asked if there would be a fence installed to
the west of Buck Brush Road, concerned that there is a potential for existing well
interference by the new development, and why gross acres can be used instead of net
acres to meet the minimum lot sizes.
Seth Lloyd, Cheyenne Planner, said that the City would like to see Buck Brush Road
expanded, not vacated, to allow the redevelopment of parcels to the east and to
provide a connection to Riding Club Road.
Casey Palma responded to remarks and said that the applicant prefers to leave the
R-O-W in place to provide access to an open space or for a trail or pedestrian
connection if needed. The gross acreage can include R-O-W since this is property
that will never be built on.
Jason Arnold said that  Buck Brush Road could be vacated  later by a petition initiated
by residents and did not need to be part of this project.
Chairman Caughey closed the hearing and called for a motion and discussion on the
Ironhorse, 3rd Filing Subdivision and Plat.
A motion was made by Mark Smith, seconded by Natacha Gaspar to
adopt the findings of fact a and b of the staff report and to recommend
approval of the Subdivision Permit and Plat for Ironhorse, 3rd Filing to the
Board of County Commissioners with no conditions. Vote 4-0.
Caughey, Stadel, Gaspar, Smith
Aye:
Watkins
Excused:
Adjournment
There being no further business Chairman Caughey adjourned the meeting at 3:55 p.m.
